From eb6ff8a20102c75cd33329ce868ee502cbc4c8c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Engineering OS TL <tl@engineering-os.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:24:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add curve_points and curve_length utils: bezier control-point
 measurement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The path attribute has exposed bezier control points since v0.11.0, but
no measurement capability used them: endpoint-only distances under-read
curved paths substantially (a quarter-arc by chord is ~10% short).

- curve_points(curve): all control points of a curve object's path, in
  path order — the full drawn geometry, recoverable in one call.
- curve_length(curve, n=32): the arc length in points — lines and closes
  contribute their euclidean lengths; each cubic segment is flattened at
  n sample points (t = k/n, direct Bernstein form) and contributes the
  chord sum. For a kappa-approximated quarter-arc of r=100 at the default
  n=32 the value is 157.08587595730572 (~4e-5 relative above the analytic
  arc — the kappa bezier deviates outward; the chord flattening inside it
  reads correspondingly low; the effects nearly cancel).

Four new tests (173 -> 177): control-point order, exact line+close
euclidean, the quarter-arc convergence with the pinned N=32 literal, and
default-n + multi-subpath summation.
